      "text": "The absence of sufficient natural light in most open-plan offices.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text never mentions natural light or lighting conditions as a concern; the focus is entirely on noise, privacy, and cognitive control, making this irrelevant and unsupported by the passage."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Employees being required to work longer hours than in traditional office setups.",  
      "why_wrong": "The passage does not discuss work hours or employee time commitments; it centers on environmental distractions and workspace design, so this claim is entirely outside the scope of the text."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "The high cost of installing soundproofing materials in office buildings.",  
      "why_wrong": "While sound-absorbing materials are mentioned as a possible solution, the text never discusses cost as a barrier or problem; this distractor misrepresents the author’s focus on structural design issues, not financial constraints."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Managers being unable to monitor employees effectively in open spaces.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text does not suggest that monitoring is a challenge or that managers lack oversight; instead, it emphasizes cognitive strain and privacy loss, not surveillance or managerial control."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "A decline in social interaction among coworkers due to excessive silence during quiet hours.",  
      "why_wrong": "The passage argues that quiet hours are insufficient, not that they reduce social interaction; in fact, it implies that collaboration is already overemphasized, making this a reversal of the author’s argument."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Employees being distracted by the sight of coworkers using personal devices during work hours.",  
      "why_wrong": "While visual distractions are mentioned, the text specifically attributes the core issue to the lack of privacy and cognitive control, not personal device use; this distractor misidentifies a minor detail as the central problem."  
    }  
  ]  
